BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucsb:4bm9i1alvfv8q302o0rc6vrcvc@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260921T194726Z
DTSTART:20261009T010000Z
DTEND:20261009T023000Z
SUMMARY:Open Source Lounge: Evening edition
LOCATION:UCSB Library room 2509 and Zoom
DESCRIPTION:Come learn about what open source software/hardware is and how
  you can get involved. Featuring guest speakers with wisdom and resources 
 for student hackers and tinkerers. Pizza will be served for in-person atte
 ndees who registered in advance.\n\nOur guest speaker for 10/8 is Alex Jen
 kins\, Computer Engineering student at Georgia Tech and founder of the Lib
 reTech Collective\, a student organization dedicated to Free\, Libre\, & O
 pen-Source software\, hardware\, and knowledge. (https://ltc.cc.gatech.edu
 /)\n\n>>> REGISTER HERE! <<<\nWhen: Thu. Oct. 8\, 2026\; 6pm-7:30pm\nWhe
 re: UCSB Library room 2509 and Zoom\nWho: Students only (grad + undergrad)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ltc.cc.gatech.edu/
END:VEVENT
